# Tune panel (F12) smoke: single 6x variant row + staged passes.
# MMPX judging concluded 2026-07-06 (s2>s3 shipped); panel is kept as the
# pass-tuning debug tool (no scheduled deletion).
# Geometry locked by test_tune_panel.h::test_script_geometry_lock (panel rect,
# variant row 0, preset rows 0/1, clear/apply). Ops-row clicks derive from the
# same layout: +f center (278,165), +a center (306,165).
# NOTE: preset-row and chip-strip click coordinates depend on the variant-row
# count (rows flow down 11 px per registered scaler; presets sit between the
# variants and the chips). Ops-row and clear/reset/apply clicks are
# bottom-anchored and safe. Re-derive preset/chip coordinates if a second
# scaler module ever registers.
# Passes are STAGED via +f/+a rather than relying on Reset-to-config: a config
# whose roger_omyac_passes tokens don't parse (e.g. numeric "2 1") yields an
# empty live pass list, which would make Clear/Reset/Apply all no-ops.
wait 4500
snap tune-baseline
key f12
wait 500
snap tune-open
click 273 31
wait 500
snap tune-variant-6x
# Known-good preset row 1 (273,55): stages + applies that pattern in one click
# (regen in memory, so allow apply-scale settle time).
click 273 55
wait 5000
snap tune-preset-applied
click 278 165
wait 300
click 306 165
wait 300
snap tune-staged
click 303 177
wait 5000
snap tune-applied
click 244 177
wait 300
click 303 177
wait 5000
snap tune-wireframe
key f12
wait 500
snap tune-closed
quit
